An agent reply that lays out labeled options or alternatives.
-- hit/agent-reply --
Two options: keep the flag or drop it.
- **Option A**: keep the old flag.
We could (a) rebase now or (b) wait for the queue.
There are three ways forward here, all cheap.
-- pass/agent-reply --
I kept the old flag, since two callers still read it.
The command takes two arguments and three flags.
Option parsing moved into its own file.
The `(a)` and `(b)` markers are the list style the page uses.
